---
// Data deletion instructions for GoteDev Analytics (the "data deletion URL" Meta's app review
// asks for). Public on purpose: `open` skips the pre-launch bounce so Meta's reviewers can read it.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { GOTEDEV_LEGAL as L, hasRealEmail } from '../lib/gotedev-legal';
---
<Layout title={`Data deletion · ${L.app}`} description={`How to have data deleted from ${L.app}.`} open>
  <section class="info">
    <h1>Data deletion</h1>
    <p><strong>{L.app}</strong>. Last updated {L.effective}.</p>
    <p>
      {L.app} is the tool Rotem Gotlieb uses to publish to and read his own Facebook Pages and
      Instagram accounts. If it holds data about you, for example because you commented on one of
      his posts, you can have it deleted.
    </p>

    <h2>How to ask</h2>
    <p>
      Email
      {hasRealEmail
        ? <a href={`mailto:${L.contactEmail}?subject=Data%20deletion%20request`} class="squiggle">{L.contactEmail}</a>
        : <span>{L.contactEmail}</span>}
      with the subject <strong>"Data deletion request"</strong>. In the message, name the account the
      request is about: your Facebook name or your Instagram username. A link to the post or comment
      helps, but is not required.
    </p>
    <p>
      The same steps cover the operator's own data: the access tokens and post records for his
      accounts are deleted the same way.
    </p>

    <h2>What is deleted</h2>
    <p>
      Everything the app holds about the named account: stored comments, the public name or username
      attached to them, and any analytics or records linked to that account. For the operator's own
      accounts, this also includes the access tokens and post records. Deletion is completed within
      {L.deletionDays} days of the request, and you will get a reply confirming it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Deleting data from the app does not remove a comment from Facebook or Instagram itself. To
      remove a comment from the platform, delete it there.
    </p>

    <h2>Removing the app's access</h2>
    <p>
      If you connected an account to {L.app}, removing the app under Facebook Settings &gt; Apps and
      Websites (or Instagram Settings &gt; Apps and websites) revokes its access. People who only
      commented never connected an account, so an email request is all that is needed.
    </p>

    <h2>More</h2>
    <p>
      How the app handles data is described in the
      <a href="/privacy/" class="squiggle">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .info { max-width: 680px; margin: 0 auto; padding: var(--s-12) var(--s-6) var(--s-24); }
  .info h1 { margin-bottom: var(--s-6); }
  .info h2 { margin: var(--s-8) 0 var(--s-2); font-size: var(--text-lg); }
  .info p { margin-bottom: var(--s-3); }
</style>
